| **Research Scope** This brief ranks nine major omni-channel retailers and platforms by the aggressiveness and effectiveness of their AI deployment in retail operations. It draws exclusively from publicly available sources including SEC filings, earnings transcripts, press releases, trade publications, industry conferences (NRF 2026, Shoptalk 2026, Groceryshop 2025), and retail podcasts. No proprietary or confidential data is included. |
| --- |

# **Executive Summary: AI Deployment Rankings**

The following tiered rankings reflect each company’s AI maturity as of March 2026, weighted across strategic vision, production deployment, measurable ROI, partnership depth, and organizational commitment.

| **Tier 1 — Leading ****&**** Scaled** |
| --- |
| **1** | **Walmart** | Most comprehensive. Four production super agents, $55M+ supply chain savings, 50% app adoption of Sparky, Google Gemini + OpenAI partnerships, dedicated EVP of AI Acceleration. Agentic commerce strategy is real and measurable. |
| **2** | **Instacart** | AI-first platform transformation. Physical AI via Caper carts on NVIDIA Jetson, enterprise AI solutions suite, NVIDIA grocery world model, 65% latency reduction. $9.85B GTV. |
| **3** | **Amazon (Grocery)** | $7B+ annual automation spend, 1M+ robots, Vulcan touch-sensitive picking, DeepFleet AI fleet coordination, Whole Foods micro-fulfillment. Infrastructure massive but grocery strategy in flux. |
| **Tier 2 — Aggressive ****&**** Scaling** |
| **4** | **Target** | $5B+ capital investment, OpenAI partnership (18K HQ employees), Trend Brain for fashion, rebuilt search/recommendations. Strong on personalization. |
| **5** | **Kroger** | New Chief Data & AI Officer (March 2026), Google Gemini agentic shopping rollout, Sage AI platform. Pivoted away from Ocado CFCs ($2.6B impairment). 84.51° data science backbone. |
| **6** | **Albertsons** | Fastest post-crisis pivot. Four explicit AI priorities, OpenAI shopping assistant (10% basket lift), Google Conversational Commerce agent, $1.5B cost-cut program. |
| **Tier 3 — Building ****&**** Investing** |
| **7** | **DoorDash** | Dot autonomous robot (live in AZ), 350K AI-powered calls/day, ChatGPT grocery integration. Strong logistics AI but grocery-specific depth limited. |
| **8** | **Ahold Delhaize** | Smart follower strategy, 5B euro savings target 2025–2028, Peapod Digital Labs, AIRlab research, W23 venture fund. Methodical but not bleeding edge. |
| **Tier 4 — Claims Exceed Results** |
| **9** | **Ocado Group** | 100+ AI applications, advanced robotics (OGRP picked 30M+ items), but 75% valuation collapse, Kroger shuttered 3 warehouses ($2.6B impairment), still not profitable. |

# **1. Walmart**

## **Strategy Overview**

Walmart has deployed the most comprehensive agentic AI strategy in retail, built around four integrated super agents serving all stakeholder groups. The strategy is production-grade with measurable ROI across supply chain, customer engagement, and workforce productivity.

## **Key Initiatives**

**Four Super Agents Platform**

- **Sparky (Customer/Shopping Agent): **Launched June 2025. 50% of Walmart app users have interacted. 35% higher AOV vs non-Sparky users. 81% use for product availability. Expanding to reordering, service booking, multimodal inputs.

- **Marty (Partner/Supplier/Advertiser Agent): **Beta for Walmart Connect sponsored search. Available to all advertisers H1 2026.

- **Associate Agent: **Centralizes resources for 1.5M store associates. AI cuts shift planning from 90 to 30 minutes. 44-language translation. VizPick AR + RFID inventory.

- **Developer Agent (WIBEY): **Unified entry point consolidating 200+ internal agents. Integrates CLI, Slack, VS Code. Single-prompt service scaffolding.

**Element ML Platform**

Proprietary foundation for all agent development. Refactored for stateful agent orchestration, tool calling, and plugin ecosystems.

**Supply Chain AI**

- **Wally (Merchant AI Agent): **Real-time inventory imbalance detection. Analyzes weather, social media, logistics. Autonomously reroutes stock. $55M+ waste savings in 2025.

- 30M delivery miles eliminated via AI route optimization

- 94M lbs CO2 avoided

- Electronic shelf labels in ~2,300 stores, full rollout to 5,200 by end 2026

- Trend-to-Product cuts fashion production lead time by 18 weeks

## **Strategic Partnerships**

- **OpenAI: **Employee training certification (launching 2026). ChatGPT Instant Checkout failed (3x worse conversion), being replaced by Sparky integration.

- **Google Gemini: **Universal Commerce Protocol, launched January 2026. Gemini includes Walmart/Sam’s products automatically. Linked accounts, sub-3-hour delivery.

## **Leadership**

- **Doug McMillon (CEO): **Headcount freeze through 2028 as AI absorbs growth.

- **Daniel Danker (EVP, AI Acceleration): **Hired July 2025 from Instacart (former CPO). Leads all product management and design.

- **Suresh Kumar (EVP, Global CTO): **Oversees new EVP of AI Platforms role.

- **Archimedes Stuk (VP, Technology): **Limited public presence. Likely internal-facing role within Agent Builders pillar.

## **Investment ****&**** ROI**

- $22B total annual capex ($19B U.S.); no AI-specific breakout disclosed

- 10,000+ new AI licenses deployed

- 26.18% YoY EPS growth attributed to AI framework

- 30% logistics cost savings, 68% higher contract success rates

- 850M+ product catalogue data points improved via GenAI

## **Analyst Commentary**

Jefferies analyst Corey Tarlowe views Walmart as less of a traditional retail corporation and more of a technology firm. Premium valuation may be justified by AI-driven operating leverage.

# **2. Kroger**

## **Strategy Overview**

Kroger is making a major AI pivot under new CEO Greg Foran (appointed February 2026), with Google Gemini-powered agentic shopping rolling out nationwide and a newly created Chief Data & AI Officer role.

## **Key Initiatives**

**Google Cloud Gemini Partnership (January 2026)**

- Meal Planning Assistant with AI-powered recommendations

- Shopping Assistant for item discovery, basket building, budget management

- Agentic capabilities: multi-step task execution from single instructions

- Nationwide rollout in progress

**Sage AI Platform**

Combines conversational, generative, and agentic AI. Powers shopping and meal planning across Kroger’s digital properties.

**Kroger Precision Marketing**

- Unified retail media, consumer insights, loyalty marketing

- AI-powered personalization across CTV, in-store, online

- New Google DV360 integration (March 2026) for YouTube attribution

- Leader: Christine Foster, SVP Commercial Strategy & Operations

**84.51° Data Science**

- Runs millions of automated ML algorithms

- President Milen Mahadevan elevated to Chief Data & AI Officer (March 6, 2026)

**Fulfillment Pivot**

- Closed 3 underperforming Ocado-built automated warehouses

- $2.6B impairment charge, $350M payment to Ocado

- Refocused on store-based fulfillment + third-party partnerships (Instacart, DoorDash, Uber)

## **Leadership**

- **Greg Foran (CEO, Feb 2026): **5 growth priorities centered on digital, AI, retail media.

- **David Kennerley (CFO): **Capital investments to support technology and AI. Introducing agentic AI shopping in 2026.

- **Milen Mahadevan (Chief Data ****&**** AI Officer, March 2026): **Previously 84.51° CEO. Reports to Yael Cosset (EVP, Chief Digital & Technology Officer).

## **Investment**

- FY 2025 capex: $3.6–$3.8B (tech/AI explicitly called out)

- $16B digital sales in FY2025 (20% Q4 growth)

- $400M ecommerce profitability gains expected 2026

# **3. Amazon (Grocery-Specific)**

## **Strategy Overview**

Amazon shut down all 57 Fresh stores and 15 Go locations (January 2026), consolidating grocery under Whole Foods with a focus on online delivery, micro-fulfillment robotics, and 100+ new Whole Foods stores.

## **Key Initiatives**

**Whole Foods Micro-Fulfillment (November 2025)**

- Plymouth Meeting, PA concept store with Fulfil ShopBot robots

- 10,000 sq ft automated facility, 12,000+ unique items

- Fulfills orders within minutes across all temperature zones

- Expansion to 100+ new Whole Foods stores planned

**Amazon Robotics Fleet**

- 1M+ robots across 300+ facilities

- **Vulcan: **First robot with sense of touch (fragile item handling)

- **DeepFleet (June 2025): **GenAI foundation model for fleet optimization, 10% better travel efficiency

- **Proteus: **28% throughput boost, 30% injury reduction, $520M+ saved in 2025

- Pick speeds up ~50%, damage claims down double digits

**Project Cremini**

- Integration of 100K+ Whole Foods employees into Amazon systems

- Enabling Amazon’s technology stack across Whole Foods operations

**Just Walk Out: De-prioritized**

Not carried forward in new grocery strategy. Replaced with fulfillment automation (robots in backrooms, not store floors).

**Rufus: Limited Grocery Integration**

General AI shopping assistant, not explicitly grocery-focused in recent announcements. 300M users reported.

## **Investment**

- $7B+ annually in automation infrastructure

- $200B total 2026 capex (all segments, not grocery-specific)

# **4. Target**

## **Strategy Overview**

Target is deploying AI aggressively across personalization, supply chain, and trend intelligence with a major OpenAI partnership and $5B+ in capital investment.

## **Key Initiatives**

**OpenAI Partnership**

- ChatGPT Enterprise for 18,000 HQ employees (supply chain forecasting, store process streamlining)

- Target app in ChatGPT with personalized recommendations, multi-item baskets, Drive Up/Pick Up/shipping

- Multi-year frontier model partnership

**Target Trend Brain**

- GenAI trend intelligence platform blending human creativity with machine intelligence

- Produces insights in hours instead of weeks (80% faster)

- Used for color, pattern, silhouette confirmation for collections

**Personalization**

- 10,000+ new AI licenses in Q2 FY2025

- Rebuilt search and recommendations for intent-based results

- 100,000+ product pages improved with GenAI

- AI-driven personalization generating billions in incremental sales

## **Leadership**

- **Michael Fiddelke (COO, incoming CEO): **AI will power merchandising authority, guest experience, and smarter advertising feedback loops.

## **Investment**

- $1–2B incremental operating investment for 2026

- $5B capital spending for supply chain, stores, technology

# **5. Albertsons**

## **Strategy Overview**

Fastest AI pivot in grocery following the failed Kroger merger. Four explicit AI priorities, multiple tech partnerships, and an AI shopping assistant already showing measurable basket lift.

## **Key Initiatives**

**Four AI Priorities for FY2026**

- Digital customer experience

- Merchandising intelligence (predictive, not reactive)

- Labor optimization (GenAI scheduling/forecasting)

- Supply chain enhancement

**AI Shopping Assistant (December 2025)**

- Powered by OpenAI

- Ask AI search: 10% increase in basket sizes

- Reduces shopping time from 45 minutes to as little as 4 minutes

- First retailer to deploy Google Cloud’s Conversational Commerce agent

**Media Collective AI**

- Capgemini partnership for media planning/operations/content

- OpenAI Ad Pilot Program participant

- 20% faster speed to market target

- Catalog optimized for LLMs for agentic commerce

## **Leadership**

- **Susan Morris (CEO, effective May 2025): **Succeeded Vivek Sankaran.

## **Investment**

- $462M capex for stores and digital/supply chain tech

- $1.5B 4-year cost reduction program enabled partly by AI

- Partnerships: Google, OpenAI, Databricks, Microsoft, Capgemini

# **6. Ahold Delhaize**

## **Strategy Overview**

Self-described “smart follower” on AI. Methodical approach targeting 5B euros cumulative savings 2025–2028 through AI and automation across logistics, distribution, store operations, and back office.

## **Key Initiatives**

**Peapod Digital Labs**

- End-to-end forecasting and replenishment AI tested at Food Lion and Hannaford, rolling across all US chains

- Cloud-based platform for picking process optimization

- AI logistics optimization: 6% delivery van km reduction (Bol online store)

**AIRlab Research**

- Partnership with Innovation Center for AI at Albert Heijn and bol.com

- Seven PhDs researching socially responsible algorithms

- Cross-geography application pathway (EU to US)

**W23 Global Venture Fund**

- Partnership with Tesco, Woolworths, Empire, Shoprite

- $125M over 5 years

- Invested in AI startups Harmonya and Protex AI (August 2025)

**Edge Retail Media Platform**

- Proprietary ad platform launched January 2026

- Agentic AI layer enabling one-click media planning/activation

## **Leadership**

- **Jan Brecht (CTO, effective September 2025): **From Nissan/Mercedes-Benz/Adidas. Hired to build next-generation digital and AI capabilities.

## **Investment**

- 5B euros cumulative savings target 2025–2028

- $125M W23 Global venture commitment (shared with 4 retailers)

# **7. Instacart**

## **Strategy Overview**

Transformed into AI-first grocery retail-tech platform. Building a “grocery world model” connecting physical store data with online commerce. New CEO Chris Rogers (August 2025) after Fidji Simo departed to OpenAI.

## **Key Initiatives**

**Enterprise AI Solutions Suite (November 2025)**

- **Cart Assistant: **AI shopping companion with meal planning

- **Store View: **Real-time shelf visibility via computer vision + Caper Carts

- **Catalog Engine: **AI catalog intelligence

- **Agentic Analytics: **AI-powered retail data insights

**Caper Smart Carts — Physical AI**

- NVIDIA Jetson Orin edge AI processor

- Item recognition, auto produce weighing, gamified quests, location-based coupons, aisle-aware advertising, EBT SNAP tracking

- 2,200+ retail banners, 100K+ locations

- 2026 UK launch via Morrisons partnership

**NVIDIA Partnership — Grocery World Model**

- NVIDIA Dynamo-Triton for item ranking and retail media

- 65% latency reduction in whole-page ranking, 40% in item ranking

**ChatGPT Integration**

First grocery partner with native checkout on ChatGPT. Partnerships span OpenAI, Google, and Microsoft.

## **Leadership**

- **Chris Rogers (CEO, August 2025): **Previously Apple (iPhone market adoption).

- **Fidji Simo (former CEO): **Left to become OpenAI CEO of Applications — signal of Instacart’s AI talent depth.

## **Performance ****&**** Investment**

- Q4 2025: GTV $9.852B (14% YoY), Revenue $992M (12% growth), Orders 89.5M (16% growth)

- Perfect order fill rate improved 5 percentage points via AI

- Engineer output up 40% from AI-assisted coding

# **8. DoorDash**

## **Strategy Overview**

Pivoting toward operating system for local commerce. AI deployed across logistics, autonomous delivery, merchant tools, and data training infrastructure.

## **Key Initiatives**

**Dot Autonomous Robot (October 2025)**

- All-electric, 30-lb capacity, 20 mph

- Vision-based with 8 cameras, radar, lidar

- Live in Tempe and Mesa, AZ; expanding

**Phone Ordering Automation**

- 350,000+ AI-powered calls/day

- 35,000+ food orders/day within 6 weeks of launch

**Merchant AI Tools**

- AI item description generator, AI camera for food photos

- Automated photo approval (1-min), inventory management via CV + LLMs

**ChatGPT Grocery Integration (December 2025)**

- Meal to Cart feature with Kroger, Safeway, Wegmans, Schnucks, etc.

- #1 third-party marketplace for U.S. grocery volume

**AI Data Training (2026)**

Couriers earn extra money filming household tasks to train AI/robotics models.

## **Leadership**

- **Tony Xu (CEO): **Driving autonomous delivery and local commerce strategy.

## **Investment**

- Several hundred million dollars more allocated for 2026 AI/tech

- Stock tumbled 8% on Q4 2025 results due to spending concerns

# **9. Ocado Group**

## **Strategy Overview**

Markets itself as an AI/robotics leader in grocery automation, but faces a critical gap between capability claims and business performance. Pivoting after major U.S. partnership failures.

## **Key Initiatives**

**AI ****&**** Robotics Systems**

- 100+ embedded AI applications across Ocado Smart Platform

- AI “air traffic control” orchestrating bot fleet (10 comms/second per bot)

- On-Grid Robotic Pick (OGRP): Computer vision, ML, smart sensors. 30M+ items picked in 2024.

- 600 Series Bot (Re:imagined product suite)

**North American Solutions Hub**

- Dallas, TX facility showcasing OSRS, Chuck AMRs, OCADEX systems

- Exclusivity contracts expired end 2025, enabling multi-retailer sales per market

## **Business Performance Reality**

- Valuation collapsed ~75% to approximately £3B

- Kroger closed 3 Ocado-built warehouses: $2.6B impairment, Ocado received $250M compensation, missing $50M revenue

- Still not profitable (expected H2 2026)

- FY25 revenue grew 12%, EBITDA up £66M to £178M

- 150M GBP cost reduction planned by FY27

## **Leadership**

- **Tim Steiner (CEO): **Announced strategic pivot to multi-market, multi-retailer post-exclusivity.

# **Conference ****&**** Industry Media Findings**

## **NRF 2026 Big Show (January 11–13, NYC)**

- Google CEO Sundar Pichai keynoted. Launched Gemini Enterprise for CX, Customer Experience Agent Studio, Universal Commerce Protocol for agentic ecommerce.

- OpenAI’s Ashley Kramer paneled on ChatGPT retail integration. Emphasized top-down + bottom-up AI empowerment.

- Agentic commerce dominated sessions: Rise of Agentic Commerce, Driving AI Intelligence into Supply Chain.

- Harris poll: 40% of users leveraged AI for shopping in December 2025.

## **Shoptalk 2026 (March 24–26, Las Vegas)**

- Sephora launched dedicated ChatGPT app with Beauty Insider integration.

- Gap Inc: First fashion company with full checkout inside Google Gemini.

- Walmart embedding Sparky inside ChatGPT and Gemini simultaneously.

- eMarketer projects 8.8% of e-commerce agentic by 2029; Merkle forecasts up to 50%.

## **Groceryshop 2025 (September 28 – October 1, Las Vegas)**

- Ahold Delhaize (Karin Chu): AI agents changing shopper entry points via ChatGPT.

- Kroger (Christine Foster): In-store retail media underutilized yet powerful.

- Albertsons (Liz Roche): Stores as full-funnel experiences.

- Uber (Susan Anderson): AI as core vision for Uber Eats.

- AI use case highlights: smart search (50%+ conversion lift), dynamic recipe planners, agentic supply chain.

## **NRA Show 2025 (May 17–20, Chicago)**

- 74% of restaurant operators planning to increase tech investment (Deloitte 2025)

- 61% prioritizing automation

- Voice AI for drive-thru/kiosk, robotic fry stations, intelligent scheduling

# **Retail Podcast ****&**** Industry Media Highlights**

## **Key Trade Publications**

- **Grocery Doppio: **AI grocery shopping shifting from search to autopilot. 70% of grocery trips digitally influenced; loyalty tied to system reliability. Practical agentic AI applications in retail media, promotions, service recovery.

- **Progressive Grocer: **Grocery’s next decade depends on purpose-built AI (Joseph Lee, Delectable AI CEO, March 2026). Retail Innovation Outlook 2026 focused on intelligent automation and agentic commerce.

- **Supermarket News: **NRF 2026 declared the agentic era. AI agents will dictate how consumers buy food (FMI Midwinter). Afresh AI platform now covers all grocery departments.

- **Grocery Dive: **Only 15% of U.S. consumers using AI for grocery shopping (Dunnhumby, February 2026). AWG deploys AI shopping assistant for 150+ independent stores.

- **Retail Brew: **AI dominated Shoptalk Spring 2026 buzz. 2026 projected as the year of zero-click buying — AI-driven ecommerce at 1.5% of online shopping, hockey stick projected.

## **Key Podcasts**

- **Retail Gets Real (NRF): **Episode 402 recorded live at NRF 2026 — agentic AI as structural change in retail.

- **Jason ****&**** Scot Show: **EP337 on agentic commerce at Citi’s Global Consumer & Retail conference (March 2026). Target reporting 40% traffic growth from AI; Amazon at 300M Rufus users.

- **Omni Talk: **Coverage of Kroger’s new CEO, the AI ad war, and Shoptalk 2026 takeaways.

- **The Retail Razor Show: **Retail Media 2026 episode with Andrew Lipsman on DSP shifts and agentic commerce.

***End of Brief***

